## 4. Interfaces

### 4.1 C3 — the census schema (the fixed extraction target)

Two layers, per SAEOS-1 §4.2 (universal envelope) and §4.3 (type facets).

**Envelope, extraction obligations (9 fields, graded for every in-scope type):**
`label`, `summary`, `provenance.origin`, `provenance.author_kind`, `provenance.source_hash`,
`evidence[]`, `valid_from`, `falsifier`, `coordinates`.

**Envelope, system-assigned at ingest (8 fields, graded `n/a`, excluded from the denominator):**
`id` (minted `sakg://…`), `type`, `namespace` (set at emission by the producing project, §6.1b rule 4),
`facets` (container), `provenance.ingested_at`, `status` (lands `candidate` by §6.1b), `confidence`
(**derived, never authored** — §4.2 invariant), `valid_until`.

Excluding these is not leniency: grading a field the spec forbids anyone to author would inflate loss
with cells that were never an extraction obligation.

**Type facets (35 fields), with their claimed PAEOS source:**

| Type | Facet fields | Claimed source |
|---|---|---|
| Decision | `problem_ref`, `options[]`, `chosen`, `rationale`, `constitutional_basis`, `decided_by_role` | decision-graph, PAEOS-9 §5.11 (`context, options[], chosen, rationale, constitutional_basis`; edges *decided-by-role*, *for-goal*) |
| Option | `label`, `description`, `considered_at`, `rejected`, `rejection_rationale` | L04 Ideation candidate set (PAEOS-9 §8.4) |
| Constraint | `kind`, `statement`, `source`, `binding_scope` | L11 frozen contract: affected files, forbidden files, acceptance criteria, rollback (PAEOS-9 §4.3, §8.4) |
| TradeOff | `axis`, `side_a`, `side_b`, `resolution`, `decision_ref` | L06 trade-off matrix (PAEOS-9 §8.4, "decision axes explicit") |
| Component | `name`, `kind`, `interfaces`, `owns_data` | architecture-graph / L08 artifact set (PAEOS-9 §5.4) |
| Scar | `failure_class`, `root_cause`, `detection_signature`, `guard_action`, `severity`, `origin_run` | scar-graph (PAEOS-9 §5.8) — **1:1 field parity with §4.3** |
| EvidenceRef | `hash`, `uri`, `kind`, `reverification_instructions`, `binding` | Evidence contract PAEOS-7.6 §6 (`hash, kind, artifact_hash, environment_hash, reproducible_command`) |

**Matrix size.** 7 types × 9 envelope obligations = 63, plus 35 facet fields = **98 cells per goal**,
294 across the sample, before `n/a` exclusions. Tractable by hand; large enough that a single
convenient grade cannot move the ratio.

**Grading granularity — one grade per (goal × type × field).** Where a goal contains several instances
of a type (e.g. four Options), the cell takes the **worst grade observed across instances**.
*Rejected alternative:* per-instance grading — a goal with twenty trivially-extractable Options would
swamp the denominator and let sample shape, not extractability, set the result.

### 4.2 C8 — the report schema (binds AC-1..AC-4)

Frontmatter (exactly one `verdict:` line, exactly one `loss_ratio:` line in the whole file):

```
  ---
  artifact: sakg-s1-extraction-probe
  spec_under_test: SAEOS-1 §9/A8
  protocol_frozen_at: <L11 plan artifact hash>
  sample_rule: <the §7.1 rule, verbatim>
  verdict: NO-GO
  loss_ratio: 0.42
  secondary_loss_ratio: 0.71
  edge_loss_ratio: 0.55
  ---
```

Per-goal section, repeated ≥3 times (each header is the AC-3 match):

```
  ## goal: <goal_id>
  seal_ref: <seal_hash>
  ceremony: trace_a | trace_b
  sources: [ledger/<...>, reviews/tasks/<...>, ...]
  goal_loss_ratio: 0.51
  goal_verdict: contributes-NO-GO

  | node_type | field | grade | locator | note |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | Decision | chosen | extractable | reviews/tasks/<f>#<anchor> | verbatim |
  | TradeOff | axis | absent | — | L06 auto-discharged (trace_a stub) |
```

Every non-`absent` cell **must** carry a locator. A grade without a locator is not a measurement, and
C5 rejects it (§6, SM-2 invariant).

Closing sections: aggregation arithmetic (§7.3 shown, not just stated), the threshold check with each
clause evaluated, secondary and edge censuses, and any incidents raised (§9).

