## 5. Data flow

```
ledger/ ─────┐
             ├─▶ C1 select ─▶ SampleSet ─▶ C2 resolve ─▶ SourceSet ─┐
reviews/tasks/┘        (deterministic)         (read-only)          │
                                                                    ▼
                                          C3 CensusSchema ──▶ C4 attempt (hand)
                                              (frozen)              │
                                                                    ▼ Cell{grade, locator, note}
                                                            C5 grade/adjudicate
                                                                    │ GradedMatrix (294 cells max)
                                                                    ▼
                                                            C6 aggregate ──▶ Ratios
                                                                    │
                                                                    ▼
                                                            C7 verdict (pure) ──▶ GO | NO-GO
                                                                    │
                                                                    ▼
                                                            C8 emit ──▶ reviews/spikes/…md
```

**Direction is strictly one-way.** No arrow returns from C6/C7 to C3 or C1 — that absence *is* the
protocol. A back-edge (re-sampling after seeing ratios, or re-scoping the schema after seeing the
verdict) is the failure mode this design exists to prevent, and SM-1 makes it a terminal `VOID`.

Nothing on this path is durable substrate: no ledger append, no CAS write, no goal transition. The
probe produces one markdown artifact and one set of incidents. It holds **no authority** — mirroring
§3.3 and §6.4's "one write path, zero authority" posture toward SAKG itself.

