## 8. Probe failure and degradation behaviour

| Condition | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| **Fewer than 3 sealed goals resolvable** | **Halt. Emit nothing. Raise an incident and remand to intake.** Writing three `## goal:` sections when only two real goals exist would satisfy AC-3 while lying. Insufficient corpus is itself an A8-relevant finding: Ω1 cannot self-populate from a corpus that does not exist yet. |
| **A sampled goal's referenced artifacts are unresolvable** | Do **not** silently substitute. Record the goal, grade its unresolvable cells `absent`, and note the resolution failure — an unresolvable artifact *is* extraction loss. |
| **Sample is single-stratum (all Trace-A or all Trace-B)** | Proceed, but the report must state that its verdict does not generalize to the other stratum, and `sample_rule:` must show why no goal of the other kind existed. |
| **Grader uncertainty on a cell** | Worse-of tie-break (§7.2). Record the ambiguity in the cell's `note`. |
| **Protocol violated after FROZEN** | `VOID` (SM-1). The probe proves nothing; re-run from a new frozen plan. |
| **`loss_ratio` computes to exactly 1.00** | See §9.3 — the acceptance contract cannot express it. Report the true value, raise the incident, verdict stays NO-GO. **Do not emit `0.99`.** |

